    {
      "description": "Why there is no ceiling line on the gauge above, and how to alert on headroom instead.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "id": 13,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**The gauge above has no ceiling line, on purpose.** `WS_MAX_CONNECTIONS` is read once at\nstartup by `configuration.ts`; the gauge is incremented and decremented at runtime. Nothing\nexports the configured value, so a hardcoded line here would be a number that is right in\nlocal and wrong in production the first time anyone tunes the env var.\n\n- Default: `1000` (`.env.example:91`, `src/config/env.validation.ts:43`).\n- The application refuses new sockets at the ceiling rather than queueing them, so the\n  symptom is refused connections with no 5xx and no error counter moving.\n- **To alert on headroom instead of eyeballing the gauge**, set a Grafana-managed alert on\n  `vortex:ws:connections` with the threshold at your configured ceiling, or add an\n  exporting metric for the limit in `src/config/configuration.ts` and reference it here.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "WS_MAX_CONNECTIONS is config, not a metric",
      "type": "text"
    }
